34	1stBank Center	11450 Broomfield Ln	Agate	CO	80021	US	39.904570	-105.085440	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 23:22:35.927261	f	\N	\N	The 1stBank Center (formerly the Broomfield Event Center) is a mid-sized indoor arena located in Broomfield, Colorado. Opening in 2006, this multi-purpose venue serves the north Denver metropolitan area with a versatile space for concerts, sporting events, and family shows. The arena features a modern design with approximately 6500 seats for concerts, though capacity can vary based on event configuration. The venue underwent significant renovations and rebranding in 2010 when Peak Entertainment took over management, transforming it into a premier concert destination for the region. The arena's location between Denver and Boulder makes it particularly accessible to audiences throughout Colorado's Front Range.	75	["Venue website","Local news archives","Concert industry databases"]	2025-07-06 21:44:37.375485	completed	[{"event":"Venue Renovation","date":"2010","description":"Major renovation and rebranding under Peak Entertainment management","category":"historical_event"}]	[{"feature":"Flexible Configuration","description":"Versatile space that can be configured for various types of events from concerts to sporting events","category":"stage"},{"feature":"Strategic Location","description":"Positioned between Denver and Boulder, serving the north metro area","category":"location"}]	f	\N
202	Brandon Amphitheater	8190 Rock Way	Brandon	MS	39042	US	32.275155	-90.023317	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-06-02 06:46:16	2025-07-06 22:01:33.097676	f	\N	\N	The Brandon Amphitheater is a modern outdoor concert venue located in Brandon, Mississippi that opened in 2018. This 8300-capacity amphitheater is situated within a 250-acre park called The Quarry and represents one of Mississippi's premier entertainment destinations. The venue features a covered seating area and spacious lawn seating, designed to provide excellent sight lines and sound quality throughout the facility.\n\nPurpose-built for live music and entertainment, the amphitheater incorporates contemporary amenities while taking advantage of its natural setting. The venue has quickly established itself as a significant stop for major touring acts in the Southeast, filling an important niche between smaller theaters and larger arenas in the region. Its location just east of Jackson makes it easily accessible while providing a more intimate concert experience than larger urban venues.\n\nSince its opening, the Brandon Amphitheater has hosted numerous notable country, rock, and pop artists, becoming an important cultural asset for central Mississippi. The venue's design includes modern concession areas, comfortable seating, and thoughtful acoustic engineering that makes it particularly suitable for outdoor performances.	85	["Official venue website","Local news coverage","City of Brandon municipal records","Concert industry databases"]	2025-07-06 22:01:33.096451	completed	[{"event":"Venue Opening","date":"2018","description":"Grand opening of the first major amphitheater in central Mississippi","category":"historical_event"}]	[{"feature":"Modern Design","description":"Purpose-built contemporary amphitheater with covered seating area and lawn seating","category":"architecture"},{"feature":"Natural Setting","description":"Located within The Quarry development with natural landscaping and park-like surroundings","category":"location"},{"feature":"Convenient Access","description":"Easily accessible location just east of Jackson with ample parking","category":"amenities"}]	\N	\N
