188	Irving Plaza	17 Irving Plaza	New York	NY	10003	US	40.734625	-73.988581	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 22:22:48	2025-07-06 22:53:33.253235	f	\N	\N	Irving Plaza is a historic music venue and ballroom located in the Union Square neighborhood of Manhattan. Originally opened in 1888 as a Victorian-style theater, the venue has evolved through multiple incarnations including time as a Polish-American community center and meeting hall before becoming one of New York City's premier music venues. The three-story, 1025-capacity venue features a main ballroom with a horseshoe-shaped balcony offering excellent sightlines of the stage.\n\nThe venue gained prominence in the 1970s and 1980s as a key player in New York's punk and new wave scenes, hosting early performances by artists like the Ramones, Talking Heads, and Bob Marley. In 1991, Live Nation (then Still Delsener) took over operations and renovated the space, helping establish it as a crucial stepping stone for emerging artists while still attracting established acts looking for an intimate NYC setting.\n\nToday, Irving Plaza remains one of Manhattan's most beloved mid-sized venues, known for its blend of historic architecture and modern amenities. The venue's combination of industrial charm, intimate atmosphere, and superior acoustics continues to make it a favorite among both performers and concert-goers. Recent renovations have updated the facilities while preserving the venue's historic character and unique features.	85	["Live Nation venue website","Billboard Magazine archives","NYC Landmarks Preservation Commission","Rolling Stone articles"]	2025-07-06 22:53:33.252861	completed	[{"event":"Bob Marley performance","date":"1976","description":"One of Marley's earliest NYC performances","category":"performance"},{"event":"U2 North American club debut","date":"1980","description":"First U.S. club show during Boy Tour","category":"performance"},{"event":"Extensive renovation","date":"2019","description":"Major modernization while preserving historic elements","category":"architectural"}]	[{"feature":"Horseshoe Balcony","description":"Distinctive wraparound balcony providing excellent sightlines","category":"architecture"},{"feature":"Historic Architecture","description":"Victorian-era details preserved throughout venue","category":"architecture"},{"feature":"Intimate Setting","description":"Multi-level venue layout creates close proximity to performers","category":"acoustics"}]	\N	\N
