173	Santa Barbara Bowl	1122 N Milpas St	Santa Barbara	CA	93103	US	34.433262	-119.693304	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:28	2025-07-06 21:58:36.58075	f	\N	\N	The Santa Barbara Bowl is a historic 4562-seat amphitheater nestled in the foothills of Santa Barbara, California. Built in 1936 as part of the Federal Works Project Administration, this iconic outdoor venue combines stunning Spanish-style architecture with breathtaking ocean and city views. The natural bowl shape carved into the hillside provides excellent acoustics and intimate sightlines despite its sizeable capacity.\n\nThe venue has undergone several major renovations while maintaining its historic character, including significant upgrades in the early 2000s that modernized facilities while preserving the original WPA-era stonework and architectural elements. The Bowl's unique setting, with its terraced seating and dramatic backdrop of mountains and sea, has made it one of the premier outdoor concert venues on the West Coast.\n\nOver its 85+ year history, the Santa Barbara Bowl has hosted countless legendary performers including Bob Dylan, The Rolling Stones, Radiohead, and many others. Today, it operates as a non-profit foundation and presents about 35 concerts per season between April and October. The venue remains central to Santa Barbara's cultural identity and is renowned for providing an incomparable concert experience that combines natural beauty with excellent sound and intimate performer-audience connection.	85	["Santa Barbara Bowl official website","Wikipedia","Santa Barbara Historical Society","Local news archives"]	2025-07-06 21:58:36.580401	completed	[{"event":"Venue Construction","date":"1936","description":"Built as part of the Federal Works Project Administration, establishing a major cultural venue for Santa Barbara","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"Major Renovation","date":"2000s","description":"Comprehensive renovation and modernization while preserving historic elements","category":"architectural"}]	[{"feature":"Natural Bowl Setting","description":"Carved into hillside providing natural acoustics and tiered sightlines","category":"architecture"},{"feature":"Ocean and Mountain Views","description":"Spectacular backdrop of Santa Barbara coastline and mountains","category":"location"},{"feature":"Historic Architecture","description":"Original Spanish-style architecture and WPA-era stonework preserved","category":"architecture"},{"feature":"Seasonal Operation","description":"Opens April through October for approximately 35 shows per season","category":"amenities"}]	\N	\N
184	Royal Arena	Hannemanns Allé 18	Aabybro	81	2300	DK	57.162500	9.730560	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:28	2025-07-06 21:59:33.382633	f	\N	\N	Royal Arena is a modern multi-purpose indoor arena located in the Ørestad South area of Copenhagen, Denmark (not Aabybro as incorrectly listed). Opened in 2017, this state-of-the-art venue serves as Copenhagen's premier large-scale indoor entertainment and sporting facility. The arena features distinctive Nordic architectural elements with its wave-like wooden facade and was designed by 3XN Architects in collaboration with HKS Architects.\n\nWith a flexible capacity system, Royal Arena can accommodate up to 16000 spectators for concerts and 12500 for sporting events. The venue was developed through a partnership between the City of Copenhagen and Realdania, with operating rights held by Live Nation Denmark. Its design emphasizes sustainability and acoustic excellence, featuring advanced sound systems and adjustable configurations to optimize the experience for different types of events.\n\nSince its opening, Royal Arena has hosted numerous high-profile concerts, sporting events, and entertainment shows, establishing itself as one of Scandinavia's leading venues. The arena has welcomed international artists like Metallica (who performed the inaugural concert), Drake, and Roger Waters, while also serving as a venue for major sporting events including the World Men's Handball Championship and Ice Hockey World Championship.	90	["Royal Arena official website","Wikipedia","Danish architectural archives","Live Nation Denmark"]	2025-07-06 21:59:33.382194	completed	[{"event":"Inaugural Concert by Metallica","date":"2017-02-03","description":"Metallica performed the first-ever concert at Royal Arena with a sold-out show","category":"performance"},{"event":"World Men's Handball Championship","date":"2019","description":"Served as one of the main venues for the 2019 World Men's Handball Championship","category":"sportin