5	Saratoga Performing Arts Center	108 Avenue of the Pines	Saratoga Springs	NY	12866	US	43.053070	-73.798730	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:26	2025-07-06 23:22:35.90898	f	\N	\N	The Saratoga Performing Arts Center (SPAC) is a prestigious amphitheater nestled within the picturesque Saratoga Spa State Park. Opened in 1966, this world-class venue serves as the summer home to both the New York City Ballet and The Philadelphia Orchestra, making it a unique cultural institution that bridges classical and contemporary performances. The amphitheater features covered seating for approximately 5200 patrons and a sprawling lawn that can accommodate up to 20000 additional guests.\n\nThe venue's distinctive architecture, designed by Arnold Aronson and Vollmer Associates, harmoniously integrates with its natural surroundings. The covered amphitheater's swooping roof design not only provides excellent acoustics but also creates an intimate atmosphere despite its large capacity. The surrounding park setting, complete with towering pines and natural springs, offers concert-goers a uniquely immersive experience that combines cultural entertainment with natural beauty.\n\nSPAC has hosted countless legendary performers across all genres, from classical virtuosos to rock icons. It has become a cornerstone of the Northeast's cultural landscape, particularly known for its summer festival season. The venue continues to maintain its reputation as one of America's premier outdoor performing arts venues, balancing its classical roots with contemporary programming that attracts diverse audiences year after year.	90	["Official SPAC website","Wikipedia","Saratoga Springs Historical Society","New York State Parks Department records"]	2025-07-06 21:41:55.58779	completed	[{"event":"Venue Opening","date":"1966-06-16","description":"First performance by New York City Ballet performing 'A Midsummer Night's Dream'","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"Philadelphia Orchestra Summer 