ocation"},{"feature":"Covered Pavilion","description":"Large covered seating area protects reserved seat ticket holders from weather while maintaining outdoor atmosphere","category":"architecture"},{"feature":"Natural Bowl Design","description":"Utilizes natural terrain for optimal sight lines and sound projection","category":"acoustics"}]	\N	\N
20	TD Garden	100 Legends Way	Boston	MA	02114	US	42.366276	-71.062188	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 21:43:02.966222	f	\N	\N	TD Garden is Boston's premier indoor arena and one of the most significant entertainment venues in New England. Opened in 1995, this modern facility replaced the historic Boston Garden and serves as home to both the NHL's Boston Bruins and NBA's Boston Celtics. The arena features a distinctive architecture that pays homage to its predecessor while incorporating contemporary amenities and technology.\n\nWith a concert capacity of approximately 19580, TD Garden has hosted many of music's biggest names and most memorable performances. The venue's multi-level seating configuration and advanced sound system make it particularly well-suited for large-scale concerts and productions. Its location in Boston's North End neighborhood, directly above North Station, makes it highly accessible via public transportation.\n\nBeyond sports and concerts, TD Garden has established itself as a cornerstone of Boston's cultural landscape, hosting major political conventions, family shows, and special events. The arena underwent significant renovations in 2019, including expanded concourses, new premium clubs, and upgraded technology, ensuring its continued relevance as a world-class entertainment destination.	90	["TD Garden official website","Wikipedia","Boston Globe archives","Delaware North company records"]	2025-07-06 21:43:02.964385	completed	[{"event":"Arena Opening","date":"1995-09-30","description":"Opened as the successor to the historic Boston Garden","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"2004 Democratic National Convention","date":"2004-07","description":"Hosted the Democratic National Convention where John Kerry accepted nomination","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"Major Renovation","date":"2019","description":"Completed $100 million renovation expanding and modernizing the facility","category":"architectural"}]