22	AFAS Live	Arena Boulevard 590	Amsterdam	NH	\N	NL	52.312322	4.944225	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 21:43:16.452259	f	\N	\N	AFAS Live (formerly known as the Heineken Music Hall) is one of Amsterdam's premier indoor concert venues, located in the Amsterdam Zuidoost district near the Johan Cruijff Arena. The purpose-built music venue opened in 2001, designed specifically to provide optimal acoustics for amplified music performances. The venue features a distinctive modern architectural design with a large main hall and flexible standing/seating configurations.\n\nThe venue was constructed to fill a gap in Amsterdam's concert infrastructure, providing a mid-sized venue between smaller clubs and larger arenas. Its design incorporated advanced acoustic engineering, including specialized wall treatments and ceiling configurations to deliver superior sound quality. The building's industrial-modern aesthetic, with its prominent glass facade and steel framework, has become a recognizable landmark in the Arena Boulevard entertainment district.\n\nSince its opening, AFAS Live has hosted thousands of national and international artists across multiple genres, establishing itself as a crucial stop on European tours. The venue is particularly noted for its versatility, able to accommodate both standing-room rock concerts and seated corporate events, while maintaining excellent sight lines and sound quality throughout the space.	85	["Official AFAS Live website","Wikipedia","Amsterdam Tourism Board","News archives about venue name change"]	2025-07-06 21:43:16.451865	completed	[{"event":"Venue Opening","date":"2001","description":"Purpose-built venue opened to fill need for mid-sized concert space in Amsterdam","category":"historical_event"}]	[{"feature":"Acoustic Design","description":"Purpose-built for amplified music with specialized acoustic treatments and configurations","category":"acoustics"},{"feature":"Flexible Configuration","description":