42	Randalls Island	20 Randall’s Island Park	New York	NY	10035	US	40.794629	-73.924455	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 21:45:35.067637	f	\N	\N	Randalls Island is a unique outdoor venue space located on Randalls Island in New York City's East River. The island serves as a major recreational facility hosting large-scale concerts and festivals, with multiple configuration options for events ranging from intimate shows to major festivals that can accommodate tens of thousands of attendees. The venue space is primarily comprised of large open fields that can be adapted for various event sizes and layouts.\n\nThe island has been a significant location for major music festivals and concerts since the 1990s, including the Electric Zoo Festival, Governors Ball Music Festival, and various other large-scale music events. Its unique positioning offers stunning views of the Manhattan skyline while providing enough space away from residential areas to accommodate large crowds and sound systems.\n\nWhat makes Randalls Island particularly special as a concert venue is its versatility and accessibility despite being an island location. Connected to Manhattan, the Bronx, and Queens by bridges, the venue offers a rare combination of urban accessibility and open space that's unusual for New York City. The grounds can be configured to host multiple stages and entertainment areas while maintaining comfortable crowd flow and necessary amenities.	75	["NYC Parks Department","Festival websites","Historical news articles","Event permit records"]	2025-07-06 21:45:35.067117	completed	[{"event":"First Electric Zoo Festival","date":"2009","description":"Launched what would become one of NYC's premier electronic music festivals","category":"cultural"},{"event":"First Governors Ball Music Festival at this location","date":"2012","description":"Major music festival relocated to Randalls Island, establishing it as primary NYC festival grounds","category":"cultural"}]	[{