44	Riverbend Music Center	6295 Kellogg Avenue	Cincinnati	OH	45230	US	39.052080	-84.418884	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 21:45:39.496408	f	\N	\N	Riverbend Music Center is Cincinnati's premier outdoor amphitheater, situated along the Ohio River about 10 miles east of downtown Cincinnati. Opened in 1984, the venue was designed by Michael Graves with acoustical design by Christopher Jaffe, featuring a distinctive contemporary architectural style that complements its riverside setting. The amphitheater serves as the summer home of the Cincinnati Symphony Orchestra while also hosting major touring acts throughout the warm weather months.\n\nThe venue consists of a covered pavilion with fixed seating and a spacious lawn area that allows patrons to bring blankets and lawn chairs, creating a casual outdoor concert experience. Its location along the river provides a unique backdrop for performances, though this proximity has occasionally led to flooding concerns during severe weather events.\n\nRiverbend has become a cultural cornerstone of Cincinnati's music scene, hosting countless memorable performances across all genres, from classical to rock, country, and contemporary pop. The venue's design specifically accommodates both amplified contemporary music and classical orchestral performances, making it a versatile facility that serves diverse audiences throughout its operating season.	85	["Cincinnati Symphony Orchestra website","Venue website","Local news archives","Historical venue documentation"]	2025-07-06 21:45:39.495303	completed	[{"event":"Venue Opening","date":"1984","description":"Opened as summer home of Cincinnati Symphony Orchestra","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"2011 Ohio River Flooding","date":"2011","description":"Severe flooding required significant repairs and renovations","category":"historical_event"}]	[{"feature":"Riverside Location","description":"Situated along the Ohio River providing scenic backdrop for performances","category":"location"},{"feature":"Hybrid Design","description":"Venue designed to accommodate both amplified and orchestral performances with specific acoustic considerations","category":"acoustics"},{"feature":"Dual Seating Options","description":"Combination of covered pavilion seating and open lawn seating for different concert experiences","category":"amenities"}]	\N	\N
47	Arenan	Mårtensdalsgatan 2-8	Stockholm	AB	\N	SE	59.300923	18.090173	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 21:45:49.328231	f	\N	\N	Arenan is a concert and event venue located in the Södermalm district of Stockholm, Sweden. The venue is part of the larger Fryshuset complex, a youth center and cultural hub that has been operating since the 1980s. The venue space serves primarily as a mid-sized concert hall and event space, hosting both local and international acts.\n\nThe venue has become particularly known within Stockholm's music scene for hosting alternative, rock, and metal concerts, as well as serving as a platform for emerging Swedish artists. Its location within the Fryshuset complex gives it a unique connection to Stockholm's youth culture and music education programs.	60	["Fryshuset website","Local concert listings","Swedish venue databases"]	2025-07-06 21:45:49.327703	completed	[{"event":"Part of Fryshuset youth center establishment","date":"1980s","description":"Venue opened as part of larger youth cultural center initiative","category":"cultural"}]	[{"feature":"Youth center integration","description":"Located within Fryshuset, one of Europe's largest youth centers, providing unique connection to local music culture","category":"location"},{"feature":"Multiple configuration options","description":"Flexible space that can be adapted for different types of events and audience sizes","category":"stage"}]	\N	\N
46	XFINITY Theatre	61 Savitt Way	Hartford	CT	06120	US	41.780215	-72.669230	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 21:45:50.999775	f	\N	\N	The XFINITY Theatre (formerly known as the Meadows Music Theatre) is Connecticut's premier outdoor amphitheater, located in Hartford's North Meadows section. Opening in 1995, the venue features a distinctive covered pavilion seating area and expansive lawn section, making it the largest outdoor music venue in New England. The amphitheater has been a cornerstone of Hartford's entertainment scene for over 25 years, hosting major touring acts during the summer concert season.\n\nThe venue combines the intimacy of a pavilion setting with the casual atmosphere of lawn seating, accommodating approximately 30000 total guests. Its covered seating area protects around 7500 patrons from the elements while maintaining excellent sightlines to the stage. The sprawling lawn area has become a popular summer gathering spot for concertgoers who enjoy bringing blankets and lawn chairs for a more relaxed concert experience.\n\nUnder Live Nation's management, the venue has established itself as a vital stop on major touring circuits, particularly for summer concert series and festivals. Its convenient location off I-91 and large parking capacity has made it a regional destination for concert fans throughout New England. While primarily a warm-weather venue operating from May through September, the theatre has hosted countless memorable performances across multiple genres, from rock and country to pop and hip-hop.	85	["Live Nation venue information","Hartford Courant archives","Connecticut tourism resources","Concert industry databases"]	2025-07-06 21:45:50.998647	completed	[{"event":"Venue Opening","date":"1995","description":"Opened as the largest outdoor amphitheater in New England","category":"historical_event"}]	[{"feature":"Covered Pavilion","description":"7500-seat covered seating area providing protection from weather 