62	Saenger Theatre	1111 Canal St	New Orleans	LA	70112	US	29.956054	-90.072828	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 21:47:13.968676	f	\N	\N	The Saenger Theatre in New Orleans is a historic atmospheric theatre that opened in 1927 as the flagship of Julian and Abe Saenger's theatre empire. The venue exemplifies the elaborate architectural style of atmospheric theatres, designed to transport audiences to a romantic Mediterranean courtyard under a star-filled night sky. Its Italian Baroque interior features intricate details, ornate sculptures, and a ceiling dotted with lights mimicking constellations.\n\nAfter suffering severe damage during Hurricane Katrina in 2005, the Saenger underwent a $52 million restoration project, reopening in 2013 with modern amenities while preserving its historic charm. The meticulous renovation restored the theatre to its original 1927 grandeur, including repairing its signature ceiling and elaborate decorative elements.\n\nToday, the Saenger serves as a premier venue for Broadway shows, concerts, comedy acts, and other live performances in New Orleans. Its exceptional acoustics, ornate architecture, and historical significance make it one of the most beloved theatrical venues in the American South. The theatre is listed on the National Register of Historic Places and continues to be a cornerstone of New Orleans' vibrant cultural scene.	90	["National Register of Historic Places","Saenger Theatre official website","New Orleans Tourism Board","Local historical records","News archives"]	2025-07-06 21:47:13.968183	completed	[{"event":"Opening Night","date":"1927-02-04","description":"Grand opening featuring the film 'Rough House Rosie' and stage performances","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"Hurricane Katrina Damage","date":"2005-08-29","description":"Severe flooding damaged the theatre, leading to its closure","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"Grand Reopening","date":"2013-09-27","description":"Reopeni