115	Foro Sol	Av. Viaducto Río Piedad y Río Churubusco	Mexico City	CMX	08400	MX	19.400000	-99.090000	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 21:52:42.606315	f	\N	\N	Foro Sol is one of Mexico City's largest and most prominent outdoor concert and sports venues, originally built in 1993 as part of the Hermanos Rodríguez racing circuit complex. The multi-purpose stadium features a distinctive horseshoe-shaped design that can accommodate both racing events and large-scale concerts, with expansive concrete grandstands providing excellent sightlines.\n\nThe venue has established itself as Mexico City's premier destination for major international touring acts, hosting countless legendary performers including Metallica, Paul McCartney, Madonna, and U2. Its massive capacity and versatile configuration have made it the go-to location for the biggest concerts and festivals in Mexico's capital, while still maintaining its role as part of the Autódromo Hermanos Rodríguez Formula 1 circuit.\n\nWith a capacity that can reach up to 65000 for concerts, Foro Sol combines the energy of a stadium show with surprisingly intimate sight lines thanks to its curved design. The venue continues to play a vital role in Mexico's live music and sporting landscape, serving as a key stop for major international tours and hosting some of the country's most important musical events and festivals.	85	["Wikipedia","Official F1 documentation","Mexican tourism resources","Concert databases","News archives"]	2025-07-06 21:52:42.605211	completed	[{"event":"Opening Concert","date":"1993","description":"Venue inauguration as a major concert facility in Mexico City","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"Mexican Baseball League Home","date":"2000-2001","description":"Served as home stadium for Diablos Rojos del México baseball team","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"Corona Capital Festival","date":"2010","description":"Began hosting one of Mexico's largest music festivals","category":"cultural"}]	[{"feature":"Horseshoe Configuration","description":"Distinctive curved grandstand design that integrates with the racing circuit while providing optimal concert viewing","category":"architecture"},{"feature":"Multi-Purpose Design","description":"Capable of hosting both major concerts and sporting events with flexible configurations","category":"stage"},{"feature":"Racing Circuit Integration","description":"Built as part of the Autódromo Hermanos Rodríguez Formula 1 circuit, offering unique venue context","category":"location"}]	\N	\N
