135	Altice Arena	Rossio dos Olivais	Lisbon	11	1990-231	PT	38.767556	-9.093749	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 23:22:35.993975	f	\N	\N	The MEO Arena (now Altice Arena) is Portugal's largest indoor venue and one of the most prominent entertainment facilities in Southern Europe. Located in Parque das Nações district of Lisbon, the arena was originally built for the Expo '98 world exhibition. The multi-purpose venue features state-of-the-art acoustics and flexible configurations that can accommodate various event types from concerts to sporting events.\n\nDesigned by Portuguese architect Regino Cruz, the arena is distinguished by its modern architecture with a distinctive shell-like roof structure and glass façade. Since its opening, it has established itself as Portugal's premier venue for major international concerts, family shows, and sporting events. The arena's location within the former Expo grounds, now a modern leisure and business district, provides excellent accessibility and stunning views of the Tagus River.\n\nThe venue has hosted countless international artists and events, becoming a crucial stop for major touring acts in Southern Europe. Its advanced technical capabilities, including sophisticated sound and lighting systems, make it particularly well-suited for large-scale productions and spectacles.	90	["Official Altice Arena website","Wikipedia","Expo '98 historical records","Portuguese tourism authority"]	2025-07-06 21:54:43.407044	completed	[{"event":"Expo '98","date":"1998","description":"Venue served as the Atlantic Pavilion during the 1998 Lisbon World Exposition","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"MTV Europe Music Awards","date":"2005","description":"Hosted the prestigious MTV Europe Music Awards","category":"performance"},{"event":"Eurovision Song Contest","date":"2018","description":"Hosted the Eurovision Song Contest, marking a significant moment in Portuguese entertainment history","category":"performance"}]	[{"feature":"Flexible Configuration","description":"Modular design allows for multiple seating arrangements and capacities","category":"stage"},{"feature":"Waterfront Location","description":"Situated along the Tagus River in the modern Parque das Nações district","category":"location"},{"feature":"Advanced Technical Systems","description":"State-of-the-art sound and lighting systems suitable for major productions","category":"acoustics"}]	f	\N
133	Hollywood Bowl	2301 Highland Avenue	Los Angeles	CA	90068	US	34.111258	-118.336438	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 21:54:19.779469	f	\N	\N	The Hollywood Bowl is an iconic amphitheater nestled in the Hollywood Hills of Los Angeles, California. Known for its distinctive shell-shaped stage canopy, the venue has been the premier outdoor cultural venue in Southern California since its opening in 1922. The natural amphitheater setting, surrounded by the Hollywood Hills, creates both stunning aesthetics and remarkable acoustics that have made it one of the most famous concert venues in the world.\n\nThe Bowl has hosted virtually every major artist and orchestra of the 20th and 21st centuries, serving as the summer home of the Los Angeles Philharmonic and hosting performances ranging from classical to pop, jazz to rock. Its signature shell has gone through several iterations, with the current design dating to 2004, featuring state-of-the-art acoustics while maintaining its iconic silhouette. The venue features tiered seating that can accommodate nearly 18000 patrons, who often enjoy picnicking before performances – a longstanding Bowl tradition.\n\nBeyond concerts, the Hollywood Bowl has become a cultural landmark that represents Los Angeles itself, appearing in numerous films and television shows. It has earned National Historic Landmark status and continues to be one of the largest natural amphitheaters in the world, attracting hundreds of thousands of visitors annually for its diverse programming and unique outdoor concert experience.	90	["Hollywood Bowl official website","Los Angeles Philharmonic Archives","National Historic Landmark Database","Wikipedia","Los Angeles Times Historical Archives"]	2025-07-06 21:54:19.778411	completed	[{"event":"First Shell Installation","date":"1929","description":"Installation of the first permanent elliptical shell, designed by Lloyd Wright","category":"architectural"},{"event":"Beatles Performance","date":"1964-08-23","description":"The Beatles performed their first and only Hollywood Bowl concert, later released as a live album","category":"performance"},{"event":"National Historic Landmark","date":"1985","description":"Designated as a National Historic Landmark for its significance in American culture","category":"historical_event"}]	[{"feature":"Iconic Shell","description":"Distinctive concentric-arch shell design providing superior acoustics and visual identity","category":"architecture"},{"feature":"Natural Amphitheater","description":"Built into a natural canyon providing excellent sight lines and natural acoustics","category":"location"},{"feature":"Picnic Areas","description":"Dedicated spaces for pre-concert picnicking, a beloved Los Angeles tradition","category":"amenities"},{"feature":"Hollywood Hills Setting","description":"Dramatic backdrop of Hollywood Hills and stunning sunset views during performances","category":"location"}]	\N	\N
134	Forest National	Avenue Victor Rousseau 208	Brussels	BRU	1190	BE	50.809992	4.326016	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 21:54:26.582516	f	\N	\N	Forest National (Vorst Nationaal in Dutch) is one of Belgium's most prominent indoor concert venues, located in the Forest district of Brussels. Opened in 1970, this multipurpose arena has become a cornerstone of Belgium's live entertainment scene, hosting thousands of major international and domestic artists over its five-decade history. The venue features a distinctive modernist architectural style typical of its era, with a practical design focused on optimal sight lines and acoustics.\n\nWith a capacity of approximately 8000, Forest National occupies a sweet spot between intimate theaters and larger arenas, making it a preferred stop for touring artists. The venue has maintained its position as Brussels' premier indoor concert facility through several renovations and technical upgrades, while preserving its characteristic atmosphere that artists and audiences have come to appreciate.\n\nThe venue continues to play a vital role in Belgium's cultural landscape, hosting around 100 events annually ranging from rock concerts to comedy shows and sporting events. Its central location in Brussels, combined with excellent transport links, has helped cement its status as a key entertainment destination in the Benelux region.	75	["Venue website","Belgian tourism resources","Concert databases","News archives"]	2025-07-06 21:54:26.58223	completed	[{"event":"Opening concert","date":"1970","description":"Venue inauguration as Brussels' premier indoor concert facility","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"Major renovation","date":"2005","description":"Significant technical and facility upgrades to modernize the venue","category":"architectural"}]	[{"feature":"Flexible configuration","description":"Venue can be adapted for various event types from concerts to sporting events","category":"stage"},{"feature":"Central location","description":"Easily accessible location within Brussels metropolitan area with good public transport links","category":"location"}]	\N	\N
136	Chickasaw Bricktown Ballpark	2 S Mickey Mantle Dr	Oklahoma City	OK	73104	US	35.464959	-97.508260	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 21:54:43.027095	f	\N	\N	Chickasaw Bricktown Ballpark is a minor league baseball stadium located in the heart of Oklahoma City's historic Bricktown district. While primarily serving as the home field for the Oklahoma City Dodgers (Triple-A affiliate of the Los Angeles Dodgers), the venue occasionally hosts concerts and other entertainment events. The ballpark opened in 1998 as part of the city's Metropolitan Area Projects (MAPS) initiative and has become a cornerstone of the Bricktown entertainment district's revitalization.\n\nThe stadium features a distinctive red brick exterior that pays homage to the warehouse architecture of the surrounding historic district. Its design includes modern amenities while maintaining a classic ballpark feel, with a seating bowl that provides intimate views and excellent sight lines. The facility includes luxury suites, club seating, and a variety of concession options.	85	["Official Oklahoma City Dodgers website","Ballpark Digest","Oklahoma City tourism resources","Local news archives"]	2025-07-06 21:54:43.026765	completed	[{"event":"Venue Opening","date":"1998-04-16","description":"Opening as part of the MAPS initiative that helped revitalize downtown Oklahoma City","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"2002 Triple-A All-Star Game","date":"2002-07-10","description":"Hosted the Triple-A All-Star Game, bringing national attention to the venue","category":"historical_event"}]	[{"feature":"Brick Architecture","description":"Red brick exterior designed to complement historic Bricktown district","category":"architecture"},{"feature":"Downtown Location","description":"Located in heart of Bricktown entertainment district with easy access to restaurants and attractions","category":"location"},{"feature":"Multiple Configuration Options","description":"Flexible space that can b