170	Toyota Amphitheatre	2677 Forty Mile Road	Wheatland	CA	95692	US	39.030752	-121.513136	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:28	2025-07-06 21:58:26.815802	f	\N	\N	The Toyota Amphitheatre (formerly Sleep Train Amphitheatre) is an outdoor concert venue located in Wheatland, California, approximately 40 miles north of Sacramento. The venue features a covered pavilion seating area and an expansive lawn section, making it the largest outdoor music venue in the Sacramento region. Situated in a rural setting surrounded by agricultural land, the amphitheater provides a unique concert experience with panoramic views of the Sierra Nevada foothills.\n\nOpened in 2000 as the Sacramento Valley Amphitheatre, this venue has become a premier destination for major touring acts during the summer concert season. The facility features modern amenities while maintaining the charm of an outdoor venue, with excellent sight lines and sound quality throughout the seating areas. Its location away from urban centers allows for an immersive concert experience without city noise interference.	75	["Live Nation venue information","Local news archives","Sacramento region tourism resources"]	2025-07-06 21:58:26.81552	completed	[{"event":"Venue Opening","date":"2000","description":"Opened as the largest purpose-built outdoor music venue in the Sacramento region","category":"historical_event"}]	[{"feature":"Rural Setting","description":"Located in agricultural area with views of Sierra Nevada foothills, providing minimal urban noise interference","category":"location"},{"feature":"Dual Seating Options","description":"Features both covered pavilion seating and open lawn seating areas","category":"amenities"},{"feature":"Large Capacity","description":"Largest outdoor concert venue in the Sacramento region with 18500 total capacity","category":"amenities"}]	\N	\N
