ine Dion Performances","date":"2016","description":"Record-breaking residency shows by Quebec's most famous musical export","category":"performance"}]	[{"feature":"Versatile Configuration","description":"Can be modified from intimate theater settings to full arena setup","category":"stage"},{"feature":"Advanced Sound System","description":"Purpose-built acoustic design optimized for both sports and concerts","category":"acoustics"},{"feature":"Central Location","description":"Located in heart of downtown Montreal with excellent public transit access","category":"location"}]	f	\N
199	PNC Arena	1400 Edwards Mill Rd	Raleigh	NC	27607	US	35.803152	-78.723178	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-05-06 17:24:48	2025-07-06 22:01:14.527914	f	\N	\N	PNC Arena is a major multi-purpose indoor arena located in Raleigh, North Carolina. Opening in 1999, this modern facility serves as the home of the NHL's Carolina Hurricanes and NC State University's men's basketball team, while also hosting major concerts and events. The arena features a distinctive design with a swooping roofline and extensive glass façade that has become a landmark in the West Raleigh landscape.\n\nThe venue offers approximately 19722 seats for basketball games, with slightly different configurations for hockey and concerts. Its flexible seating arrangements and modern amenities make it one of the premier entertainment venues in the southeastern United States. The arena includes luxury suites, multiple concession areas, and state-of-the-art sound and lighting systems optimized for both sporting events and concerts.\n\nSince its opening, PNC Arena has hosted numerous high-profile concerts from artists including Bruce Springsteen, Taylor Swift, and Paul McCartney, as well as major family shows and other entertainment events. Its location near the intersection of Edwards Mill Road and Wade Avenue provides convenient access from downtown Raleigh and the surrounding region, with ample parking for large events.	90	["PNC Arena official website","Wikipedia","NHL.com","News \\u0026 Observer archives"]	2025-07-06 22:01:14.52731	completed	[{"event":"Arena Opening","date":"1999-10-29","description":"Official opening of the arena with NHL game between Carolina Hurricanes and New Jersey Devils","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"2004 NHL Stanley Cup Finals","date":"2004","description":"Hosted Stanley Cup Finals games as home venue for Carolina Hurricanes","category":"historical_event"}]	[{"feature":"Flexible Configuration","description":"Arena features adjustable seating arrangements for diffe