2	The Cynthia Woods Mitchell Pavilion	2005 Lake Robbins Dr	The Woodlands	TX	77380	US	30.161472	-95.463916	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:26	2025-07-06 23:22:35.90702	f	\N	\N	The Cynthia Woods Mitchell Pavilion, located in The Woodlands, Texas, is one of the premier outdoor amphitheaters in the United States. Opening in 1990, the venue was named after Cynthia Woods Mitchell, wife of The Woodlands founder George Mitchell, and stands as a testament to their vision for combining arts and community development. The pavilion was designed by architectural firm Horst Berger Partners with a distinctive tensile membrane roof structure that has become an iconic landmark in the region.\n\nThe venue features a covered seating area and an expansive lawn section, creating a versatile space that hosts both contemporary concerts and classical performances. As the summer home of the Houston Symphony, it maintains a unique dual identity as both a popular music venue and a center for performing arts. The pavilion underwent a significant renovation in 2009, enhancing its facilities and expanding its capacity to accommodate larger audiences.\n\nToday, the pavilion ranks consistently among the world's top amphitheaters in ticket sales and hosts approximately 65 events per season, drawing over 500000 visitors annually. Its location within The Woodlands' Town Center, surrounded by trees and adjacent to The Woodlands Waterway, provides a distinctive setting that combines natural beauty with modern amenities.	90	["Official Pavilion Website","The Woodlands Township records","Houston Symphony documentation","Local news archives","Billboard venue rankings"]	2025-07-06 21:41:42.691553	completed	[{"event":"Venue Opening","date":"1990-04-27","description":"Opened with a performance by the Houston Symphony Orchestra","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"Major Renovation","date":"2009","description":"Underwent significant renovation and expansion, including improved facilities 