mium Amenities","description":"72 suites, 9 lounges, and multiple premium club spaces","category":"amenities"},{"feature":"Location Integration","description":"Connected to Kansas City Power \\u0026 Light District entertainment area","category":"location"}]	f	\N
108	Canalside	44 Prime Street	Buffalo	NY	14202	US	42.881330	-78.877560	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 23:22:35.976235	f	\N	\N	The Erie Canal Harbor, now commonly known as Canalside, is an outdoor entertainment venue and historic waterfront district in downtown Buffalo, New York. Located at the western terminus of the historic Erie Canal, this revitalized area has been transformed into a vibrant public space that hosts concerts and cultural events. The venue features a large open-air performance area along the Buffalo River, with the city's industrial heritage and restored canal infrastructure providing a unique backdrop for live entertainment.\n\nThe site has undergone significant redevelopment since the 2000s as part of Buffalo's waterfront revitalization efforts. What was once a largely abandoned industrial area has been reimagined as a premier entertainment destination, featuring both a concert venue and public gathering space. The venue hosts the popular Canalside Live concert series during summer months, drawing thousands of visitors to enjoy live music against the backdrop of Buffalo's waterfront and historic grain elevators.\n\nThe venue's location and layout make it particularly notable for outdoor concerts, with its open-air setting providing views of Lake Erie and downtown Buffalo's skyline. The space has become central to Buffalo's cultural renaissance, hosting both major touring acts and local performers while maintaining strong connections to the area's maritime and industrial heritage.	75	["Buffalo Place","Visit Buffalo Niagara","Erie Canal Harbor Development Corporation","Local news archives"]	2025-07-06 21:51:54.306161	completed	[{"event":"Canalside development project completion","date":"2010","description":"Major waterfront redevelopment project transformed the area into an entertainment destination","category":"historical_event"}]	[{"feature":"Waterfront Setting","description":"Located along Buffalo's historic waterfront with views of Lake Erie and grain elevators","category":"location"},{"feature":"Historic Canal Infrastructure","description":"Incorporates restored elements of the original Erie Canal terminus","category":"architecture"},{"feature":"Flexible Space","description":"Large open-air venue space that can be configured for various event sizes","category":"stage"}]	f	\N
127	Maine Savings Amphitheater	1 Railroad St	Bangor	ME	04401	US	44.793329	-68.774659	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 23:22:35.987856	f	\N	\N	Darling's Waterfront Pavilion is an outdoor amphitheater located along the Penobscot River in downtown Bangor, Maine. The venue is part of the larger Waterfront Park complex and has become northern Maine's premier destination for large outdoor concerts since its opening in 2010. The open-air venue features a permanent stage structure with lawn seating that slopes down toward the water, offering views of both the performances and the river.\n\nThe venue has established itself as a significant stop for major touring acts during Maine's summer concert season, typically operating from June through September. Its riverside location in downtown Bangor has helped revitalize the city's waterfront district and drives significant tourism to the region. The pavilion hosts everything from country music festivals to rock concerts, typically drawing audiences from across Maine and neighboring New England states.\n\nAs the largest outdoor music venue in northern Maine, it plays an important role in the region's cultural landscape, bringing major touring artists to an area that historically had limited access to large-scale live music events. The venue's success has contributed to Bangor's growing reputation as a cultural destination and has helped establish the city's waterfront as a major entertainment district.	85	["Local news archives","Venue website","City of Bangor records","Concert industry databases"]	2025-07-06 21:53:44.432401	completed	[{"event":"Venue Opening","date":"2010","description":"Establishment of first major outdoor concert venue in northern Maine","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"Waterfront Revitalization","date":"2010-2022","description":"Venue played key role in transforming Bangor's waterfront into entertainment district","category":"cultural"}]	[{"feature":"Riverside Location","d