132	Sutter Health Park	400 Ballpark Dr	Sacramento	CA	95691	US	38.580203	-121.514039	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 23:22:35.991795	f	\N	\N	Raley Field, now known as Sutter Health Park, is primarily a baseball stadium located in West Sacramento, California that occasionally hosts concerts and other entertainment events. Opened in 2000, this 14014-capacity venue serves as the home field for the Sacramento River Cats minor league baseball team. The ballpark features views of the Sacramento skyline and Tower Bridge across the Sacramento River, creating a distinctive backdrop for both sporting events and concerts.\n\nThe venue was built to replace the aging Scottsdale Park and represents a significant investment in West Sacramento's waterfront development. Its design incorporates modern amenities while maintaining an intimate, family-friendly atmosphere. The stadium features a 360-degree concourse that allows visitors to walk completely around the venue while maintaining views of the field.\n\nWhile primarily known for baseball, the venue has demonstrated versatility in hosting various entertainment events, including concerts and community gatherings. Its location along the Sacramento River and proximity to downtown makes it an accessible and scenic destination for both sports and entertainment experiences.	90	["Official venue website","Sacramento River Cats official site","Local news archives","West Sacramento city records"]	2025-07-06 21:54:07.710162	completed	[{"event":"Venue Opening","date":"2000-05-15","description":"Official opening of the ballpark, marking significant development in West Sacramento's riverfront area","category":"historical_event"}]	[{"feature":"Sacramento Skyline View","description":"Offers panoramic views of the Sacramento skyline and Tower Bridge across the Sacramento River","category":"location"},{"feature":"360-Degree Concourse","description":"Complete wrap-around concourse allowing full venue circulation while