153	Falconer Salen	Falkoner Alle 7	Copenhagen	84	\N	DK	55.679459	12.533369	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:28	2025-07-06 23:22:36.004365	f	\N	\N	The Falkoner Center (now known as Falconer Salen) is a historic entertainment venue located in the Frederiksberg district of Copenhagen, Denmark. Originally opened in 1958, it has served as one of Copenhagen's premier concert and theater venues for over 60 years. The venue is housed within a larger complex that historically included a hotel and conference facilities.\n\nThe venue has undergone several transformations over its lifetime, including major renovations in 2016 when it became part of the Scandic Hotels group. The current concert hall features excellent acoustics and maintains much of its mid-century modern architectural character while incorporating contemporary amenities.\n\nToday, Falconer Salen continues to be an important cultural institution in Copenhagen, hosting a mix of concerts, theatrical performances, and corporate events. Its central location and versatile space make it a significant venue in Denmark's entertainment landscape.	70	["Danish cultural websites","Hotel chain information","News articles about renovation"]	2025-07-06 21:56:25.624412	completed	[{"event":"Major Renovation","date":"2016","description":"Comprehensive renovation when acquired by Scandic Hotels group","category":"architectural"}]	[{"feature":"Central Location","description":"Located in the heart of Copenhagen's Frederiksberg district","category":"location"},{"feature":"Versatile Space","description":"Can be configured for various types of events from concerts to corporate functions","category":"stage"}]	f	\N
180	Sunshine Grove	12517 NE 91ST Ave	Okeechobee	FL	34972	US	27.359491	-80.730703	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:28	2025-07-06 23:22:36.020796	f	\N	\N	The Okeechobee Music and Arts Festival is a multi-day camping and music festival held at Sunshine Grove in Okeechobee, Florida. Launched in 2016, this 800-acre venue transforms into a temporary entertainment city featuring multiple stages, art installations, and immersive experiences. The festival grounds include wooded areas, open fields, and a beach along Lake Okeechobee, creating distinct environments for different types of performances and activities.\n\nThe venue is specifically designed to accommodate large-scale festival operations while maintaining a natural, outdoor atmosphere. Its layout includes the main Be Stage, the Here Stage, Jungle 51 (a late-night electronic music area), and Aquachobee Beach, among other performance spaces. The site's natural typography and vegetation are incorporated into the festival design, creating unique viewing areas and acoustic environments.\n\nWhile primarily known for hosting the annual Okeechobee Music & Arts Festival, Sunshine Grove serves as a private events venue during other times of the year. The festival has featured notable performers across multiple genres, from electronic and hip-hop to rock and indie, establishing itself as one of the Southeast's premier music festivals.	85	["Festival official website","News coverage from Billboard and Rolling Stone","Local Florida news archives","Festival attendance reports"]	2025-07-06 21:59:10.8994	completed	[{"event":"Inaugural Okeechobee Music \\u0026 Arts Festival","date":"2016-03","description":"First edition of the festival featuring Mumford \\u0026 Sons, Kendrick Lamar, and Skrillex","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"COVID-19 Impact","date":"2020","description":"Festival cancelled due to pandemic, returned in 2022","category":"historical_event"}]	[{"feature":"Multiple Environmental Zones","description":"Venue includes wooded areas, open fields, and beachfront on Lake Okeechobee","category":"location"},{"feature":"Jungle 51","description":"Dedicated wooded area for late-night electronic music programming","category":"stage"},{"feature":"Aquachobee Beach","description":"Beach stage area along Lake Okeechobee featuring daytime programming","category":"stage"},{"feature":"Camping Infrastructure","description":"Extensive camping facilities with designated areas for different camping experiences","category":"amenities"}]	f	\N
189	Merriweather Post Pavilion	10475 Little Patuxent Pkwy	Columbia	MD	21044	US	39.208933	-76.862619	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-25 00:31:40	2025-07-06 23:22:36.028629	f	\N	\N	Merriweather Post Pavilion is a renowned outdoor music venue situated in Symphony Woods, Columbia, Maryland. Designed by the acclaimed architect Frank Gehry and opened in 1967, it was originally built as the summer home of the National Symphony Orchestra. The pavilion features a distinctive hyperbolic paraboloid roof design that has become iconic in concert venue architecture.\n\nThe venue has evolved from its classical music roots to become one of the premier outdoor amphitheaters in the United States, hosting countless legendary performers across all genres. Its intimate yet expansive design, set within 40 acres of preserved woodland, creates a unique concert environment that combines natural acoustics with park-like ambiance. The pavilion underwent a major renovation in 2017 as part of a $55 million project that modernized facilities while preserving its architectural character.\n\nToday, Merriweather Post Pavilion stands as a cultural landmark in the Mid-Atlantic region, regularly ranking among the top amphitheaters in the country. Its significance extends beyond music, as it played a crucial role in James Rouse's vision for Columbia as a planned community where culture and nature could coexist harmoniously.	90	["Official Merriweather Post Pavilion website","Wikipedia","Columbia Association historical records","Baltimore Sun archives","Downtown Columbia Arts and Culture Commission"]	2025-07-06 22:00:05.309907	completed	[{"event":"Venue Opening","date":"1967","description":"Opened as summer home of National Symphony Orchestra","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"Grateful Dead Performances","date":"1970s-1980s","description":"Multiple legendary performances by the Grateful Dead made the venue a famous stop on their tours","category":"performance"},{"event":"Major Renovation","date":"2017","description":"$55 million renovation project to modernize facilities","category":"architectural"}]	[{"feature":"Frank Gehry Design","description":"Distinctive hyperbolic paraboloid roof design by renowned architect Frank Gehry","category":"architecture"},{"feature":"Natural Setting","description":"Set within 40 acres of preserved woodland known as Symphony Woods","category":"location"},{"feature":"Acoustic Design","description":"Natural amphitheater setting with excellent sound projection characteristics","category":"acoustics"}]	f	\N
194	Huntington Bank Pavilion at Northerly Island	1300 S Linn White Drive	Chicago	IL	60605	US	41.861580	-87.609250	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-25 03:22:44	2025-07-06 23:22:36.030548	f	\N	\N	The Huntington Bank Pavilion at Northerly Island (formerly FirstMerit Bank Pavilion and Charter One Pavilion) is Chicago's premier outdoor amphitheater located on the man-made peninsula of Northerly Island along Lake Michigan. This open-air venue features stunning views of both Lake Michigan and the Chicago skyline, creating a unique concert atmosphere that blends urban and natural environments.\n\nThe venue opened in 2005 and has established itself as a major summer concert destination in Chicago. The pavilion features a state-of-the-art stage and sound system, with a combination of fixed covered seating and general admission lawn space. Its location on Northerly Island, formerly the site of Meigs Field airport, provides a picturesque setting that sets it apart from other urban venues.\n\nThe pavilion has hosted numerous notable acts across various genres, from rock and pop to electronic and country music. Its lakefront location creates a distinctive concert experience, though it also means the venue operates seasonally, typically from June through September. The venue has undergone several renovations and improvements since its opening, including expanded capacity and enhanced amenities.	85	["Live Nation venue website","Chicago Park District records","Chicago Tribune archives","Local news coverage"]	2025-07-06 22:00:28.36398	completed	[{"event":"Venue Opening","date":"2005","description":"Opened as Chicago's primary outdoor amphitheater on former Meigs Field airport site","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"Major Renovation","date":"2013","description":"Significant expansion and renovation that dramatically increased capacity","category":"architectural"}]	[{"feature":"Lakefront Location","description":"Situated on Northerly Island with views of both Lake Michigan and Chicago skyline","category":"location"},{"feature":"Hybrid Seating","description":"Combination of covered pavilion seating and open lawn space","category":"amenities"},{"feature":"Weather Considerations","description":"Unique lakefront location can create dramatic weather effects and cooling lake breezes","category":"location"}]	f	\N
81	St. Joseph's Health Amphitheater at Lakeview	490 Restoration Way	Syracuse	NY	13209	US	43.088414	-76.222915	\N	\N	\N	\N	other	active	\N	"[]"	2018-03-24 20:58:27	2025-07-06 23:22:35.956761	f	\N	\N	The St. Joseph's Health Amphitheater at Lakeview (formerly Lakeview Amphitheater) is a modern outdoor concert venue located on the western shore of Onondaga Lake in Syracuse, New York. Opened in 2015, this 17500-capacity venue was built as part of a larger environmental restoration project for the formerly industrial lakefront area. The amphitheater features a distinctive curved roof design that mirrors the natural contours of the lakeshore, while providing excellent acoustics and protection from the elements.\n\nThe venue was constructed at a cost of $50 million and represents a major investment in Syracuse's cultural infrastructure. Its design incorporates both fixed seating and a spacious lawn area, offering visitors panoramic views of Onondaga Lake while enjoying performances. The facility has quickly established itself as Central New York's premier outdoor concert destination, attracting major touring acts during the summer concert season.\n\nThe amphitheater is notable for its environmental consciousness, built on remediated industrial land as part of the larger Onondaga Lake cleanup initiative. Its location and design reflect a successful blend of cultural venue development with environmental restoration, making it a symbol of Syracuse's revitalization efforts.	90	["Syracuse.com news archives","Onondaga County official records","Visit Syracuse tourism materials","Local news coverage"]	2025-07-06 22:02:36.15747	completed	[{"event":"Venue Opening","date":"2015-09-03","description":"First concert held at the venue featuring Miranda Lambert","category":"historical_event"},{"event":"Environmental Restoration","date":"2015","description":"Built on remediated industrial land as part of Onondaga Lake cleanup project","category":"historical_event"}]	[{"feature":"Lakefront Location","description":"Situated on the western shore of Onondaga Lake, offering panoramic water views","category":"location"},{"feature":"Curved Roof Design","description":"Distinctive architectural element that mirrors the natural shoreline and provides weather protection","category":"architecture"},{"feature":"Mixed Seating Options","description":"Combination of covered fixed seating and open lawn areas for different viewing experiences","category":"amenities"}]	f	\N
